This repository contains no third-party source code. The executable JAR it builds
is a Spring Boot archive, which bundles its dependencies under BOOT-INF/lib; each
of those artifacts carries its own licence and notice inside it. The dependency
tree is declared in pom.xml and package-lock.json, and

    ./mvnw org.codehaus.mojo:license-maven-plugin:2.6.0:add-third-party \
        -DexcludeTransitiveDependencies=false

writes the whole list, with licences, to target/generated-sources/license.

At the time of writing that list is Apache-2.0 and MIT almost throughout, with
EPL-2.0, EDL/BSD, and a few artifacts offered under more than one licence
(Logback under EPL-2.0 or LGPL-2.1; the Jakarta APIs under EPL-2.0 or GPL-2.0
with the Classpath Exception; JNA and Javassist under Apache-2.0 among others).
Nothing in the tree is under a licence that would restrict how this project may
be licensed.
